 "why": "GeoNames models a city as its administrative seat where Wikidata models it as the municipality, so P1566 lands on an item with no sitelink while the article sits one P131 hop away. Munich is the clearest case: P1566=2867714 is on \"Kreisfreie Stadt Muenchen\", not on the city.",
 "the_guard": "a parent article is accepted ONLY if its title, with a parenthetical or comma qualifier stripped and diacritics folded, equals one of the city's own names - its GeoNames name, its ASCII name, or its recorded name in any language. Without that, one P131 hop from a village would borrow its municipality's readership, which is a city-name swap.",
